epcs_ctrl.v (qmegawiz altasmi_parallel) has 1-cycle register latency
from CTRL.{read,write,wren,sec_erase,rd_status} input to busy_wire
assertion (read_reg → read_wire → do_read → busy_wire combinational
chain).  If NEORV32 issues the subsequent STATUS poll's bus_stb at
the cycle immediately after the CTRL store completes, the wrapper
samples am_busy=0 (stale) and wait_not_busy() returns immediately —
firmware then pulses shift_bytes before the megafunction has actually
entered the operation, the pulse is lost, and the subsequent
wait_data_valid() hangs forever.  This is the leading NH1 hypothesis
for the deterministic mode 'P' hang (2/2 byte-identical 340 B
captures, hang location wait_data_valid).

Fix: add a bounded busy-rise spin (cap at 64 iters so degenerate-fast
operations don't hang us if busy came and went) before the busy-fall
wait.  Drop-in change — all wait_not_busy() callsites benefit
(epcs_read pre-amble, epcs_read post-deassert, epcs_read_status,
epcs_erase_sector pre/post, epcs_program_page pre/post + per-byte).

Size: 14460 → 14480 B (+20 B).  Cross-tests still green (lutcodec
127/127, edits.bin 5/5).  HW validation pending — listener-first
flash of neorv32_demo.rbf + neorv32_imem_image rebuild, then 'P'.

If mode 'P' works post-fix → NH1 confirmed.  If still hangs → NH1
refuted, move to NH2 (rublock-vs-asmiblock device-arch contention)
or NH3 (JTAG-volatile vs EPCS-cold-boot pin state).
---
 sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c b/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c
index c0b7fad..0625fcd 100644
--- a/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c
+++ b/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c
@@ -61,6 +61,21 @@ static inline uint32_t am_status(void) { return *WB_AM_STATUS; }
 
 static inline void wait_not_busy(void)
 {
+    /* Two-phase wait to dodge a 1-cycle race window in altasmi_parallel.
+     * The megafunction has 1-cycle register latency from CTRL.read (or
+     * write/wren/sec_erase/rd_status) input to busy_wire assertion
+     * (epcs_ctrl.v `read_reg` → `read_wire` → `do_read` → `busy_wire`).
+     * If NEORV32 issues this STATUS poll's bus_stb at the cycle
+     * immediately after the CTRL store completes, the wrapper samples
+     * am_busy=0 (stale) and we'd skip the wait entirely — corrupting
+     * the subsequent shift_bytes pulse because the megafunction hasn't
+     * actually entered the operation yet.  First-phase: bounded spin
+     * for busy-rise (cap at 64 iters so degenerate-fast operations
+     * don't hang us if busy already came and went).  Second-phase:
+     * wait for busy-fall as before. */
+    for (int i = 0; i < 64; i++) {
+        if (am_status() & STATUS_BUSY) break;
+    }
     while (am_status() & STATUS_BUSY) { }
 }
 
